I saw the Narnia movie today.  It was excellent!  I've
never read the Narnia tales, but the movie may inspire
me to do so.  I found it much more entertaining than
the latest Harry Potter movie (which I found juvenile,
disjointed, unbalanced, and only mildly entertaining).

Also, I couldn't help but notice all the Nethack
related items in Narnia.  Tons of them!  I'm thinking
now that the origininators of Nethack (and it's
ancestors) got some of their imagery from C. S. Lewis's
Narnia tales, as well as Moorcock and Tolkien.

The Narnia movie had in it:

 1. Altars and sacrifices
 2. Death by turning-to-stone
 3. Undeath by spell of "stone to flesh"
 4. Statues
 5. A blessed +100 potion of full healing
 6. Centaurs
 7. Minotaurs
 8. Giants
 9. Trolls
10. Orc-like creatures
11. Dwarves
12. Chain mail, daggers, bows, swords, halberds, etc.
13. A magic portal

Any Nethacker should feel right at home while watching
this movie.

